# Anthropic API Key for AI features
# Get your key at: https://console.anthropic.com/
# Without an API key, the app will use random name suggestions from the existing catalog
VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-api03-...

# Groq API Key — client side (legacy useAI image-naming feature)
# Get your key at: https://console.groq.com/
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# Groq API Key — SERVER side, used by /api/fotosintesis-ai
# Must NOT have the VITE_ prefix so it stays out of the browser bundle.
# Falls back to VITE_GROQ_API_KEY if unset, but prefer a dedicated server key.
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# Optional override for the Fotosynthia model (default: llama-3.3-70b-versatile)
# Other free tier choices: llama-3.1-8b-instant, llama-3.2-90b-vision-preview
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile

# Google Sheets Integration (for centralized inventory management)
# 1. Create a Google Cloud Project: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 2. Enable Google Sheets API
# 3. Create an API Key (restrict to Sheets API only)
# 4. Create a spreadsheet and get its ID from the URL
#    Example: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/YOUR_SHEET_ID_HERE/edit
# 5. Make the spreadsheet public or share with your service account
VITE_GOOGLE_SHEETS_API_KEY=AIza...
VITE_GOOGLE_SHEETS_ID=1abc...xyz

# ─── Los dos libros de Google Sheets (AMBOS obligatorios) ────────────────────
# Desde 2026-08-11 NO tienen fallback: si faltan, api/_lib/constants.js grita en
# el arranque y envenena el valor con MISSING_ENV_<NOMBRE> para que la lectura
# falle en vez de servir otro libro. Antes caían en legacy #3 y en la SOT v2, y
# la app respondía con datos del libro equivocado sin un solo log.
#
# Hoy los dos apuntan al MISMO libro, la SOT v3. Están separados porque cumplen
# papeles distintos y podrían divergir en staging.

# Catálogo público + Asesores + Modelo-Precios.
SPREADSHEET_ID=1oRw1KSh8L1CyjUnD_D1S8a3J3ewJ_V8lN1BFR-7Bv9U

# SOT del inventario Fotosíntesis. Es ESTA —no SPREADSHEET_ID— la que decide qué
# celdas lee el pull hoja→Convex, así que debe apuntar al mismo libro donde esté
# instalado el Apps Script de sync (ver docs/runbooks/fotosintesis-convex-sync.md).
FOTOSINTESIS_SPREADSHEET_ID=1oRw1KSh8L1CyjUnD_D1S8a3J3ewJ_V8lN1BFR-7Bv9U

# ─── Convex backend (the production data store) ──────────────────────────────
# Convex hosts invitations, product views, the Fotosíntesis admin and the
# published catalog. There are TWO URLs that MUST point at the same deployment:
#
#   VITE_CONVEX_URL  — FRONTEND. Enables the ConvexProvider + reactive reads
#                      (src/lib/convex-safe.ts). When set, the UI reads
#                      invitations / guest pricing / published catalog from Convex.
#   CONVEX_URL       — SERVER (Vercel /api). Enables the API's Convex WRITE path
#                      (api/_lib/convex-client.js).
#
# ⚠️ COHERENCE RULE: set CONVEX_URL wherever you set VITE_CONVEX_URL, to the SAME
# value. If only VITE_CONVEX_URL is set, the UI reads from Convex while the API
# writes to Sheets → new invitations / guest pricing silently never appear.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment.convex.cloud
CONVEX_URL=https://your-deployment.convex.cloud

# 💸 LOCAL DEV: leave BOTH of the above EMPTY unless you are specifically working
# on something Convex-backed.
#
# The free tier's Database I/O cap is per TEAM, summed across every project and
# deployment — a dev deployment burns the same pool production does. In the
# Aug 2026 window the dev deployment alone accounted for 66.56 MB (5.5% of the
# 1 GB cap) while nothing was even shipped from it.
#
# With both unset, `convexReady` is false (src/lib/convex-safe.ts:16) and EVERY
# useConvexQuery becomes a no-op, so the app opens zero subscriptions. Catalogs
# fall back to the spreadsheet via /api/get-treasure-sheets + gviz, which is the
# documented policy: "Dev = hoja, no Convex" —
# docs/specs/2026-07-21-convex-nuevo-proyecto-tm-sot.md §2.
# Consumption analysis: docs/audits/2026-08-12-convex-usage-audit.md §6.
#
# NOTE: with them unset the Fotosíntesis admin, invitations and vitrinas have no
# backend locally. Point them at the DEV deployment (never prod) only while you
# need those, then unset again.

# Optional kill-switch. Leave UNSET for normal Convex operation. Set to "sheets"
# to force the legacy Google Sheets write path (e.g. an incident rollback) even
# when CONVEX_URL is present.
# DATA_SOURCE=sheets

# Cloudinary Configuration (legacy - for image URL optimization only)
# Note: All new media is stored in Google Drive
# Cloudinary URLs from legacy data are still optimized for delivery
# Cloud name: dyam6g2os (configured in code)
# Upload functionality has been removed - use Google Drive API instead
